==Abstract==

This document specifies a hard fork that replaces Bitcoin's fixed maximum block weight of 4,000,000 weight units with a limit that is recomputed for every block from the median weight of recent blocks. The limit for the next block is the larger of a short-window median (about 90 days of blocks) and a long-window median (about 365 days of blocks), multiplied by a constant, bounded below by the current limit and above by an absolute cap. The block signature operation cost limit scales in proportion to the block weight limit. The algorithm is an adaptation of the adaptive block size algorithm used by the Nexa blockchain.

